<speak>
<s>This is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">29062026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Two days after a US-brokered de-escalation, Israel bombed a Hezbollah tunnel in southern Lebanon — and told Washington first.</s> <s>The deal lets Israel hold a security zone while deciding on its own what counts as a violation, an arrangement only one side polices.</s> <s>Whether Lebanon's army or Hezbollah answers will test how long a ceasefire can last when enforcement runs in one direction.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>In Karachi, families gathered at the Press Club to demand criminal charges after at least nine children died and two hundred were infected with <sub alias="H I V">HIV</sub> at a government hospital.</s> <s>Only Sindh's health secretary can register a case under the Disposable Syringes Act, and a year on, none has been filed.</s> <s>The families are now appealing to <sub alias="Unicef">UNICEF</sub> and the International Labour Organization, because at home no one has been held to account.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>More than sixty-eight thousand people remain missing in Venezuela after back-to-back earthquakes of magnitude seven point two and seven point five killed at least one thousand four hundred and thirty.</s> <s>The UN Development Programme puts the damage at six point seven billion dollars, falling on an economy already strained by sanctions.</s> <s>That seventy-two-hour rescue window has passed, and whether pledged aid reaches the worst-hit zones is the open question.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Iraq's Counter Terrorism Service raided Baghdad's Green Zone overnight, arresting forty-seven people including a deputy oil minister Washington sanctioned in May for routing Iraqi crude to Iran-backed militias.</s> <s>For years the fortified zone has been the untouchable heart of Iraqi power, rarely entered by the security forces.</s> <s>Several suspects fled before troops arrived, leaving open how far this purge will actually reach.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Drone fragments killed three people and wounded eight schoolgirls in El Obeid, the besieged capital of Sudan's North Kordofan.</s> <s>Strikes have cut fuel, water and bread, and petrol now sells for one hundred and sixty thousand pounds a gallon on the black market.</s> <s>Rapid Support Forces displaced nearly four thousand people from seven North Darfur villages, deepening a war the world has largely stopped watching.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>A senior figure at the Russian International Affairs Council urged China to deepen trade with Moscow without regard to Western secondary sanctions.</s> <s>Those measures work by making third parties — here, Chinese banks — police themselves, and Russia is publicly lobbying Beijing to stop.</s> <s>Whether Chinese lenders comply will test if American financial reach can still price in the cost of dealing with a sanctioned state.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Even with the US and Iran halting strikes, the head of Japan's Nippon Yusen shipping line says clearing mines from the Strait of Hormuz will take months.</s> <s>Ships now follow two narrow corridors carrying less than half the pre-war volume, with no timeline for full clearance.</s> <s>A fifth of the world's seaborne oil moves through that strait, and diplomacy can stop the strikes, but it can't sweep a minefield.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>An Aramco helicopter crashed on Sunday near the Ras Tanura oil terminal in Saudi Arabia, killing fourteen Saudi nationals.</s> <s>The terminal had only resumed crude loadings on Friday after a four-month halt, and the cause remains unknown.</s> <s>Saudi authorities have opened an investigation, with no link yet established to the wider tensions across the Gulf.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Southeast Asian nations still have no collective answer to American tariffs imposed under Section three hundred and one, a law that lets Washington act unilaterally.</s> <s>Negotiating one by one, members lose the leverage a unified bloc of more than six hundred million people could hold.</s> <s>No ASEAN summit has produced a joint response, and each bilateral deal struck alone makes a common front harder to build.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>A reanalysis of a burial at Arene Candide in Italy finds deliberate mourning rituals from twenty-seven thousand five hundred years ago — the oldest material evidence of grief we have.</s> <s>Grave goods and the careful treatment of a teenage boy's body show symbolic care for the dead reaching deep into the Upper Paleolithic.</s> <s>It means archaeologists can now read interior emotional life from stone-age remains, without a single written word.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Russian researchers at the Gamaleya Institute say they'll finish trials of a new adult tuberculosis vaccine by the end of next year and register it in twenty twenty-seven.</s> <s>The century-old <sub alias="B C G">BCG</sub> shot protects infants but poorly shields adults from the pulmonary form that kills more than a million people a year, mostly in the Global South.</s> <s>No peer-reviewed efficacy data has been published yet, so the promise rests for now on the developer's word.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A new study in The Cryosphere finds human-caused warming is responsible for one-fifth of the retreat of West Antarctica's Pine Island glacier.</s> <s>It's the first attribution research on an Antarctic glacier, separating emissions from natural variability across eighty years of melt.</s> <s>Pine Island and neighbouring Thwaites together drive nearly half the continent's contribution to sea-level rise, raising the floor on what's already locked in.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Springer's editor-in-chief has called the retraction of two Max Planck physics papers a mistake.</s> <s>Historians suspect an algorithm flagged them as duplicates, wrongly applying modern self-plagiarism rules to a pre-digital era when wide republication was normal.</s> <s>The publisher declined to explain further, leaving scholars to wonder how much of the scientific record automated systems might quietly rewrite.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>The Electronic Frontier Foundation is warning that America's proposed Kids Act would require age checks to reach much of the internet, with a vote due within days.</s> <s>There's no privacy-preserving way to prove everyone's age at scale, so platforms will default to ID uploads or facial scans for all users.</s> <s>A law framed around child safety would, in practice, build an identity layer over the open web and end online anonymity.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Researchers report that collaborative robots paired with structured-light scanners now beat humans at traceable factory measurement.</s> <s>Every reading is logged to a permanent digital history, the kind of auditable provenance manual workflows simply can't provide.</s> <s>The same chain-of-custody logic now fought over in software supply chains is arriving on the factory floor, though live, closed-loop quality control is still unproven.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>EU negotiators have relaunched a once-shelved plan to scan private messages, meeting behind closed doors this week.</s> <s>Client-side scanning breaks encryption by design, because detecting flagged content means inspecting every message, opening a backdoor for every user.</s> <s>The draft would impose warrantless scanning orders, echoing the same surveillance-by-default logic now spreading across both sides of the Atlantic.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>